# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Copy to .env.local for `next dev`. Neither variable has a default: a default would hide a
# misconfiguration, and these two are exactly what makes one image serve many deployments.
#
# In a real deployment Helm renders PAIGASUS_ZONES from the SAME values block as the ingress
# rules, so the routing and the console's zone map cannot drift (ADR-0017).

# This app's zone id. Must equal the `zone` passed to createNextConfig() in next.config.ts.
PAIGASUS_ZONE=gateway

# Every deployed zone, mapped to its path prefix behind the single origin. The entry for
# PAIGASUS_ZONE must equal this image's compiled basePath, or the first request fails loudly.
PAIGASUS_ZONES={"iam":"/iam","gateway":"/gateway"}

# discovery's service map. This zone cannot run without an "iam" entry (it calls IAM's gRPC port
# for every session) and is pointless without a "gateway" entry (the overview reports the
# gateway's own discovery state) -- lib/config.ts refuses either entry being absent.
PAIGASUS_SERVICES={"iam":"http://iam.internal:8080","gateway":"http://gateway.internal:8080"}

# This example declares TWO zones, and a multi-zone deployment cannot use the memory session
# store: @paigasus/auth's createAuthRuntime throws on it when PAIGASUS_ZONES names more than one
# zone. PAIGASUS_SESSION_STORE has no default either, so the configuration parse rejects its
# absence before createAuthRuntime ever runs, and "redis" requires the URL below.
PAIGASUS_SESSION_STORE=redis
PAIGASUS_SESSION_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# THESE TWO VARIABLES ARE NOT ENOUGH TO RUN `next dev` (SMA-641). Six more have no default, two of
# them schema-enforced https URLs, and the app needs a real OIDC provider, an IAM gRPC endpoint and
# two service-info endpoints on the other end. NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS cannot come from this file at
# all: Node reads it while it starts, before Next loads .env.local.
#
# Run the dev stack instead. It starts the fakes, Redis and a TLS terminator, and starts both zones
# itself with the environment they need:
#
#   pnpm --dir ts dev:stack
